      "title": "Applying the Vector Form of the Chain Rule to a Function of Three Variables"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "2fc80c1f-c6e3-542f-b93e-31e38dec304b",
      ":question/problem": "If $f(x,y,z)=- 3 x z \\ln{\\left(y \\right)}$ and $\\mathbf{r}(t)=(t^{2})\\,\\mathbf{i}+(t)\\,\\mathbf{j}+(t^{3})\\,\\mathbf{k},$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(\\mathbf{r}(t))].$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
