      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The chain rule in vector form states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(\\mathbf{r}(t))]=∇f(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot {\\mathbf{r}}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $∇f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3 x z \\ln{\\left(y \\right)})\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3 x z \\ln{\\left(y \\right)})\\,\\mathbf{j}+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(3 x z \\ln{\\left(y \\right)})\\,\\mathbf{k} \\\\  & =(3 z \\ln{\\left(y \\right)})\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\left(\\frac{3 x z}{y}\\right)\\,\\mathbf{j}+(3 x \\ln{\\left(y \\right)})\\,\\mathbf{k}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute $x=\\left(t - 2\\right)^{2},y=t - 2,$ and $z=\\left(t - 2\\right)^{3}$ into the above to find $∇f(\\mathbf{r}(t)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(\\mathbf{r}(t)) & =(3 \\left(t - 2\\right)^{3} \\ln{\\left(t - 2 \\right)})\\,\\mathbf{i}+(3 \\left(t - 2\\right)^{4})\\,\\mathbf{j}+(3 \\left(t - 2\\right)^{2} \\ln{\\left(t - 2 \\right)})\\,\\mathbf{k}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $\\mathbf{r}(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\mathbf{r}}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\left(t - 2\\right)^{2})\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t - 2)\\,\\mathbf{j}+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\left(t - 2\\right)^{3})\\,\\mathbf{k} \\\\  & =(2 t - 4)\\,\\mathbf{i}+(1)\\,\\mathbf{j}+(3 \\left(t - 2\\right)^{2})\\,\\mathbf{k}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(\\mathbf{r}(t))] & =∇f(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot {\\mathbf{r}}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =((3 \\left(t - 2\\right)^{3} \\ln{\\left(t - 2 \\right)})\\,\\mathbf{i}+(3 \\left(t - 2\\right)^{4})\\,\\mathbf{j}+(3 \\left(t - 2\\right)^{2} \\ln{\\left(t - 2 \\right)})\\,\\mathbf{k})\\cdot ((2 t - 4)\\,\\mathbf{i}+(1)\\,\\mathbf{j}+(3 \\left(t - 2\\right)^{2})\\,\\mathbf{k}) \\\\  & =(3 \\left(t - 2\\right)^{3} \\ln{\\left(t - 2 \\right)})\\cdot (2 t - 4)+(3 \\left(t - 2\\right)^{4})\\cdot (1)+(3 \\left(t - 2\\right)^{2} \\ln{\\left(t - 2 \\right)})\\cdot (3 \\left(t - 2\\right)^{2}) \\\\  & =(3 \\left(t - 2\\right)^{3} \\left(2 t - 4\\right) \\ln{\\left(t - 2 \\right)})+(3 \\left(t - 2\\right)^{4})+(9 \\left(t - 2\\right)^{4} \\ln{\\left(t - 2 \\right)}) \\\\  & =3 \\left(5 t^{4} \\ln{\\left(t - 2 \\right)} + t^{4} - 40 t^{3} \\ln{\\left(t - 2 \\right)} - 8 t^{3} + 120 t^{2} \\ln{\\left(t - 2 \\right)} + 24 t^{2} - 160 t \\ln{\\left(t - 2 \\right)} - 32 t + 80 \\ln{\\left(t - 2 \\right)} + 16\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$"
